course: dictionary
lesson: 10160
title: Thunderclouds and stormy moods
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A thundercloud is a huge, tall, dark cloud that brings thunder, lightning and heavy rain. Look at the words around it in «Tall, dark, towering thunderclouds can bring lightning, heavy rain, hail and strong wind.» Tall, dark and towering all describe the cloud, so you can picture it before you even read the rest.
explain: Writers also use weather to show feelings. In «a face like a thundercloud», the face is not really a cloud. The writer means the person looks very angry, as dark and threatening as a storm. Ask yourself: what does the weather stand for here?
explain: When you see thunderclouds in real life, a safety rule matters most. Get indoors, and stay away from water and tall trees. The word thundercloud tells you that danger is near.
fact: A thundercloud is a huge, tall, dark cloud that brings thunder, lightning and heavy rain.
fact: Scientists often call a thundercloud a cumulonimbus cloud, because it grows very tall.
fact: «Thunderclouds» can bring storms, hail and strong winds.
fact: In stories, a thundercloud can stand for a coming danger or an angry mood.
fact: «A face like a thundercloud» means someone looks very angry.
exercise: «Tall, dark, towering thunderclouds can bring lightning, heavy rain, hail and strong wind.» What can thunderclouds bring? | Snow drifts across the beach | *Lightning and heavy rain | Gentle sunshine and warm breezes | Rainbows and sweet smells
exercise: Jamie says, «Her face was a thundercloud when she heard the news.» What does this mean? | She was cold and wet from the rain | She was hungry and tired | She was singing happily | *She looked very angry
exercise: What should you do if you see thunderclouds coming? | Go and stand under the tallest tree | *Get indoors, away from water and tall trees | Run to the top of the hill | Stay by the lake to watch
test: «The sky grew dark as thunderclouds gathered.» What is the writer warning us is coming? | *A storm | Snow in summer | A rainbow | A picnic in the park
test: Find the word in «Tall, dark, towering thunderclouds» that tells you the cloud is very high. | dark | thunderclouds | tall | *towering
exam: What is a thundercloud? | *A huge, tall, dark cloud that brings thunder, lightning and heavy rain | A small, white cloud that floats on a sunny day | A bright light in the night sky | A mist that rises from the sea
